###Step 3: Finding the perimeter

Side $\overline{CD}$ is perfectly horizontal, so we can use the $x$-coordinates of its endpoints to see that this side is $6$ units long.

Using the lengths of $\overline{AB}$ and $\overline{BC}$, we can find the perimeter of pentagon $ABCDE$:

$\begin{align}
\text{Perimeter} &= AB+BC+CD+DE+EA
\\\\
&= \tealE{\sqrt{85}}+\goldE{5}+6+\goldE{5}+\tealE{\sqrt{85}}
\\\\
&=16+2\sqrt{85}
\end{align}$
